source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: A cell keeps reading past a forced newline, so Jira renders both markers as items of one list inside the cell; jiro reads one physical row per cell and warns that the cell's list is kept as text.
-- input.jira --
||h||
|* a\\
* b|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><ul>
	<li>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" /></li>
	<li>b</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
| h |
| --- |
| \|\* a\\\\ |

- b|
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "table",
    "Reason": "Jira renders a list inside this table cell; JFM keeps its text"
  }
]
